Batch invariance for the GDN_ATTN backend (Qwen3.5/3.6 linear attention).

Upstream PR vllm-project/vllm#45819, still open at vLLM v0.34.0. Taken as the
runtime-file diff of its head 1991cc4f59 (2026-11-05, which merged main
14d147a7a0 into the branch) against its merge base with v0.34.0, with one hunk
re-applied by hand: v0.34.0 gathers the prefill initial state with
gather_initial_states() and grew a separate FlashInfer prefill branch, so the
per-request batch-invariant loop sits in the Triton/FLA branch. The PR pins the
GDN prefill backend to Triton/FLA whenever VLLM_BATCH_INVARIANT is set, so the
FlashInfer branch (auto-selected on Hopper) is never taken with this patch.

The PR now reads sequence boundaries from host-side metadata lists
(non_spec_query_start_loc_cpu, prefill_query_start_loc_cpu), so the
device-to-host sync our former 0002 patch removed from CUDA graph capture no
longer happens; 0002 was retired at this rebase.

